// Cycle of Life: Realistic Fauna — The Critter Pack (thecritterpack).
//
// Small ambient wildlife: songbirds, waterfowl, ground litter invertebrates, rodents, a hedgehog and
// a yak. Most follow the vanilla pattern (the male carries the spawn conditions, females and young
// ride along as companions), so one species per animal.
//
// The brown owl needs no entry: it is tagged habitat-air without habitat-land, so the mod's own
// aquatic/aerial tag filter drops it automatically.
//
// TWO STRUCTURAL NOTES:
//   * The four squirrel colours (brown, darkbrown, black, red) are one animal split across four
//     species keys by coat. Each gets a quarter of the density we want for "squirrels" so the four
//     together read as one normal population.
//   * The "_flying" / "_f" birds (crow_flying, robin_flying, house-sparrow_f, waxwing_f) are the
//     mod's ambient flyers. They spawn thickly by design (a 0.02-0.035 chance versus 0.0001 for most
//     things), so they are given fast, cheap r-strategist lifecycles rather than being throttled —
//     background birdlife should stay background birdlife.
//
// Body weights are set throughout: the mod leaves most of them unset, and weight now drives forage
// demand, grazing range, roaming speed and the satiation reserve pool.
//
// VERIFICATION STATUS: the species keys in this file were derived from the mod's own entity
// JSON (its spawn conditions and variant axes), not read off a live server roster — this mod
// is not installed on the pack author's server. A key that turned out wrong does not break
// anything: an overlay entry that matches no species is simply ignored, and the animal keeps
// its auto-discovered values. If you run this mod, `/col species` (or the roster dumped to the
// server log at startup) lists the authoritative keys, and anything mistyped here will be
// absent from it. Corrections welcome.
{
  "species": {

